  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, the most critical design question is whether multimodal fusion (RNA + image) provides a meaningful advantage over unimodal approaches — the core hypothesis of this study. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) directly tests this question while using the simplest, most standard components at each level (PCA for RNA, ResNet50 for image, single profile, concat fusion), minimizing confounding variables. This establishes a performance reference for the multimodal direction: if it performs well, subsequent experiments can explore richer encoders (scvi, scgpt), multi-profile aggregation, and alternative fusion; if it underperforms, follow-up experiments can isolate whether the bottleneck is the fusion strategy, encoder choice, or the data itself. Choosing a simple, well-understood multimodal baseline over a complex one ensures the first data point is interpretable and maximally informative for guiding the next several experiments under a tight budget."
}

